Now car model edits in vehicles.js. Need to add windows, adjust wheels, add chrome exhaust, maybe increase car scale? Let's edit.

Current code:
```js
  // glass cabin
  const cabin = new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.BoxGeometry(W * 0.82, cabinH, cabinL), glassMat);
  cabin.position.set(0, bodyY + bodyH / 2 + cabinH / 2, cabinZ);
  cabin.castShadow = true;
  group.add(cabin);
```
Add window planes after. Compute cabinY.

```js
const cabinY = bodyY + bodyH/2 + cabinH/2;
const winW = W*0.66, winH = cabinH*0.78;
const windows = [];
const addWin = (w,h,rotY,x,y,z) => { const p=new THREE.PlaneGeometry(w,h); p.rotateY(rotY); p.translate(x,y,z); windows.push({geo:p}); };
addWin(winW, winH, 0, 0, cabinY, cabinZ + cabinL/2 + 0.02); // front faces +z (plane default +z)
addWin(winW, winH, Math.PI, 0, cabinY, cabinZ - cabinL/2 - 0.02); // rear faces -z
addWin(cabinL*0.72, winH, Math.PI/2, W*0.412, cabinY, cabinZ); // right side faces +x
addWin(cabinL*0.72, winH, -Math.PI/2, -W*0.412, cabinY, cabinZ);
group.add(new THREE.Mesh(mergeLocal(windows), glassMat));
```
But glassMat transparent opacity .92 and depthWrite default true; planes may z-fight with cabin box sides (offset 0.02 outside). Fine. Side windows at x=±0.412W = ±0.816 for W=1.98, cabin half width 0.812; 0.004 outside. Good.

Wheels x: `sx * (W / 2 + 0.01)`. For merged too. Also increase wheel radius? dims sport .38; okay.

Add chrome exhausts in chromeEntries:
```js
const chromeEntries = [];
chromeEntries.push({geo: cylAt...}) 
```
No cylAt import in vehicles; use CylinderGeometry rotateX(PI/2) at rear.
```js
const exhaust = new THREE.CylinderGeometry(0.09,0.09,0.28,8).rotateX(Math.PI/2).translate(±W*0.28,0.36,-L/2-0.05)
```
Cylinder axis Y -> rotateX(PI/2) axis Z. Good. Add chrome mesh.

Add rear diffuser dark box.

Add roof scoop? no.

Add paint stripe? maybe.

Also add windshield wiper? no.

Add "MADOUT" text decal on sides? skip.

Let's edit.

